(HALVERD INSTRUMENTS, INC.) Tj
T*
(Quarterly Report — Second Quarter, Fiscal Year 2026) Tj
T*
(Quarter ended 30 April 2026. Reported 21 May 2026.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SUMMARY) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Revenue for the second quarter was $31.2 million, an increase of 8 percent against the) Tj
T*
($28.9 million reported in the second quarter of fiscal 2025. Gross margin was 58.4) Tj
T*
(percent, down 110 basis points year over year, reflecting expedited freight on PT-40 die) Tj
T*
(shipments and the initial cost of the HX-9 firmware remediation programme. Operating) Tj
T*
(income was $4.1 million. Net income was $3.3 million, or $0.19 per diluted share.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We are reaffirming full-year fiscal 2026 revenue guidance of $118 million to $124 million) Tj
T*
(and full-year gross margin guidance of 58 to 60 percent.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Two matters dominate this report and are discussed in full below: the HX-9 depth drift) Tj
T*
(defect, for which we have recorded a warranty accrual this quarter, and the single-source) Tj
T*
(position on the PT-40 pressure transducer die.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Halverd Instruments is a fictional company. This document was written to demonstrate retrieval software and describes no real business, product, person or transaction.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
