(SEGMENT RESULTS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Subsea Sensing revenue was $19.4 million, up 11 percent year over year, carried by the) Tj
T*
(HX-9 and HX-11 depth and conductivity instruments and by a full quarter of the Vessel) Tj
T*
(Integration Kit introduced in the first quarter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Industrial Calibration revenue was $11.8 million, up 3 percent year over year. Growth here) Tj
T*
(remains slower than the segment plan we set in November, and we now expect Industrial) Tj
T*
(Calibration to finish the year at the low end of its range.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Backlog at quarter end was $46.7 million, of which $29.3 million is scheduled to ship in) Tj
T*
(fiscal 2026.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(CUSTOMER CONCENTRATION) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Trondsen Offshore AS accounted for 41 percent of second-quarter revenue, up from 34) Tj
T*
(percent in the second quarter of fiscal 2025. Trondsen operates four survey vessels and) Tj
T*
(has standardised on the HX-9 for depth reference. No other customer accounted for more) Tj
T*
(than 9 percent of revenue in the quarter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We regard this concentration as our single largest commercial risk. A deferral or) Tj
T*
(cancellation by Trondsen would have a material effect on quarterly revenue and on the) Tj
T*
(full-year range given above.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
