(HX-9 DEPTH DRIFT — DESCRIPTION AND PROVISION) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In March 2026 a customer reported that HX-9 units held at depth for extended periods) Tj
T*
(returned depth values that drifted upward over time. Our engineering review confirmed the) Tj
T*
(behaviour and traced it to an accumulator overflow in the pressure-compensation routine of) Tj
T*
(firmware releases 4.2.0 through 4.4.1. Affected units drift by up to 1.8 metres after) Tj
T*
(approximately 900 hours of continuous submersion. The drift is gradual and does not) Tj
T*
(trigger the instrument's own fault flag, which is why it was not caught in qualification.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A corrected firmware release, 4.4.2, entered controlled release on 6 May 2026. Units in) Tj
T*
(the field can be updated over the vessel link; units in inventory are being updated before) Tj
T*
(shipment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We estimate the affected population at 3,100 units, being all HX-9 instruments shipped) Tj
T*
(with firmware 4.2.0 or later between June 2024 and April 2026. We have recorded a warranty) Tj
T*
(accrual of $2.4 million in the second quarter, covering firmware deployment, field) Tj
T*
(engineering time and the replacement of units that cannot be updated remotely.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Management believes this accrual reflects our current best estimate and is sufficient to) Tj
T*
(cover the affected population. No recall is planned.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
