(SUPPLY — PT-40 PRESSURE TRANSDUCER DIE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Every instrument in the Subsea Sensing segment depends on the PT-40 pressure transducer) Tj
T*
(die. The PT-40 is supplied to us by a single vendor, Tessin Micro Fabrication Ltd, under a) Tj
T*
(supply agreement that expires on 31 January 2027. Tessin manufactures the die on a legacy) Tj
T*
(150 millimetre line at one site. We hold approximately eleven weeks of PT-40 inventory.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(An interruption at that site, or a failure to renew the agreement on acceptable terms,) Tj
T*
(would stop production of every Subsea Sensing product within one quarter. We consider this) Tj
T*
(the most serious operational risk carried by the business.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We have identified a second source, Kaldbakur Semiconductor hf, and received first samples) Tj
T*
(in February 2026. Electrical characterisation of those samples is complete and within) Tj
T*
(specification. Qualification is not finished: the samples have not yet passed the) Tj
T*
(1,000-hour pressure-cycling test or the salt-fog corrosion test, and we have not yet run a) Tj
T*
(production lot. Kaldbakur is therefore identified and sampled but not qualified, and no) Tj
T*
(Kaldbakur die is in any shipped product.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We are targeting completion of qualification during the third quarter of fiscal 2026.) Tj
T*
(Until it completes, the single-source exposure described above is unmitigated.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
